\ The same loops written with named locals. A local can be used any number of
\ times, inside `if` branches and inside quotations.

\ Not tail recursive: the multiply runs after the recursive call returns.
: fact
  (forall ρ; ρ n:Int^many -- ρ r:Int^many)
  locals { n } { n 0 prim = [ 1 ] [ n 1 prim - fact n prim * ] if };

: fib-loop
  (forall ρ; ρ a:Int^many b:Int^many n:Int^many -- ρ r:Int^many)
  locals { a b n } { n 0 prim = [ a ] [ b a b prim + n 1 prim - fib-loop ] if };

: fib
  (forall ρ; ρ n:Int^many -- ρ r:Int^many)
  locals { n } { 0 1 n fib-loop };

\ Partial allocation, one request: left = remaining - min, allocated = min.
: allocate-partial
  (forall ρ; ρ remaining:Int^many requested:Int^many -- ρ left:Int^many allocated:Int^many)
  locals { remaining requested }
  { remaining requested prim <
    [ 0 remaining ]
    [ remaining requested prim - requested ] if };

\ Sort three values ascending. Nested `if`s whose branches push several locals.
: sort3
  (forall ρ; ρ a:Int^many b:Int^many c:Int^many -- ρ x:Int^many y:Int^many z:Int^many)
  locals { a b c }
  { a b prim <
    [ b c prim <
      [ a b c ]
      [ a c prim < [ a c b ] [ c a b ] if ] if ]
    [ a c prim <
      [ b a c ]
      [ b c prim < [ b c a ] [ c b a ] if ] if ] if };

\ A block's names are off the stack for its body: `swap` exchanges the two
\ values below `a`, not `a` and the value below it.
: swap-below
  (forall ρ; ρ x:Int^many y:Int^many z:Int^many -- ρ p:Int^many q:Int^many)
  locals { a } { swap };

\ A word whose effect has no row, like `add2`, takes the whole stack. Inside a
\ `locals` block it sees only the values pushed for it: the block's names are
\ off the stack, so `n`, still to be used, is not in its way.
: add2 ( a:Int^many b:Int^many -- r:Int^many ) prim + ;

: add-then-keep
  ( x:Int^many n:Int^many -- r:Int^many s:Int^many )
  locals { x n } { x 1 add2 n };

: add-in-block
  ( x:Int^many n:Int^many -- r:Int^many )
  locals { x n } { x locals { y } { y n add2 } };
